{
  "bead": "wb-gxd7.1",
  "statement": "[GPC-FEEDBACK-CONTRACT-AUDIT-R1] No Pi surface shall collapse two gp hashes into one identity because they share the `graphpolicy.snapshot.c1:` prefix or a hex suffix: each gp identity is carried verbatim under its producer field name with its profile or form tagged (`identities.graph`, `canonical_digest`, `receipt.input_snapshot`/`graph_digest`, checkpoint), compared only byte-equal within one profile/form, and old interpretations are kept until GP publishes a migration (D-IDENT-1 descriptor unshipped, gated) — docs/programs/feedback-contract-audit-2026-10-21/README.md:42@0107c72992f3",
  "quote": "- Do not collapse logically different hashes because they have the same suffix or share a prefix; preserve old identity interpretation until migration is explicitly designed.",
  "citation": "docs/programs/feedback-contract-audit-2026-10-21/README.md:42@0107c72992f3",
  "authority": "Do not change the meaning of `graphpolicy.snapshot.c1:` in place or silently rewrite old journal records.",
  "posture": "Pi holds no gp identity (0 gp hits at d75b68d1)",
  "codeFacts": [
