    "lines": {
      "README.md:42": "- Do not collapse logically different hashes because they have the same suffix or share a prefix; preserve old identity interpretation until migration is explicitly designed.",
      "01-finding-inventory.md:9": "| F01 | [one snapshot, three graph digests](../../../new-feedback/2026-10-21-one-snapshot-file-carries-three-graph-digests-graph-check-identity-inspect-graph-canonical-and-eval-input-snapshot-and-none-equals-another.md) | CONFIRMED-OPEN at `61fda0c`; current rerun owed | RC-IDENT |",
      "01-finding-inventory.md:10": "| F02 | [one theta, two checkpoint identities](../../../new-feedback/2026-10-21-one-theta-has-two-checkpoint-identities-the-cli-receipt-hashes-program-digest-plus-parameters-the-library-receipt-hashes-the-words-alone.md) | CONFIRMED-OPEN at `61fda0c`; current rerun owed | RC-IDENT / RC-STORE |",
      "02-contract-audit.md:24": "| `gp graph check` → `identities.graph` | GraphDataIR whole-document canonicalization with `GRAPH_DATA_SNAPSHOT_C1_PROFILE` | Document/profile identity | Deterministic for the same logical document under that pinned profile; not interchangeable with the projection digest |",
      "02-contract-audit.md:25": "| `gp inspect graph` → `canonical_digest` / declared `digests.canonical` | `snapshotDigestPayload` and `DATA_DIGEST_PROFILE` | DataIR projection digest | Source projection excludes fields not selected by that payload; shares the `graphpolicy.snapshot.c1:` prefix with a different preimage, so consumers must name the profile explicitly |",
      "02-contract-audit.md:26": "| `gp eval` → `receipt.input_snapshot`; `gp sample` / decision-journal snapshot binding | SHA-256 of the exact presented graph bytes (for RPC sample, compact `JSON.stringify(graph)` bytes) | Byte-exact invocation/journal join key | Whitespace and serialization affect the hash. Do not substitute a canonical document/projection hash into an existing journal link |",
      "02-contract-audit.md:30": "**Decision D-IDENT-1 (open):** publish a versioned identity descriptor whose typed fields include domain, hash algorithm, canonical profile, payload/view, and value. Alternatives: (a) additive fields/metadata that leave existing digest strings unchanged; (b) a versioned new namespace plus migration. Do not change the meaning of `graphpolicy.snapshot.c1:` in place or silently rewrite old journal records.",
      "02-contract-audit.md:38": "| `ts/src/function-ir/checkpoint.ts` / CLI named `--checkpoint` | digest of `{program_digest, parameters}` under checkpoint words profile | Logical policy identity is program-bound |",
      "02-contract-audit.md:39": "| `ts/src/evaluator/evaluate.ts` → `checkpointIdentity(theta)` | digest of the parameter words alone | Library evaluator uses a different identity for the same theta |",
      "02-contract-audit.md:40": "| `ts/src/artifact-store/cas.ts` `put(\"checkpoint\", bytes)` | canonical artifact-byte hash under a store kind | Stored blob address may differ from the logical checkpoint identity |",
      "02-contract-audit.md:42": "**Decision D-IDENT-3 (open):** choose whether evaluator receipts should expose the program-bound logical checkpoint identity, a distinct explicitly named theta-words identity, or both. Every consumer must know what the field binds. Re-pinning a golden vector requires a versioned migration if the preimage/meaning changes.",
      "02-contract-audit.md:52": "**Decision D-STORE-1 (open):** specify a total resolution relation from `(program identity, parameter words, logical checkpoint identity)` to a stored artifact address and its canonical bytes. Prefer a single store API or explicit immutable binding record. Only equate the logical digest and CAS blob hash if a proven canonical preimage theorem and tests show actual equality; do not assume equality from similar names.",
      "03-developer-workplan.md:112": "- Any supposed identity equivalence based only on a shared prefix: stop until preimages/fixtures demonstrate equivalence.",
      "ts/src/data-ir/digests.ts:23": " * (`graphpolicy.snapshot.c1:<hex>`, the GPR-1430 namespace form) and `digests.source` is carried",
      "ts/src/data-ir/digests.ts:100": "/** `graphpolicy.snapshot.c1:<hex>`: the form `digests.canonical` must carry (GPR-1042, GPR-1430). */",
      "ts/src/cli/graph-check.ts:143": "    graph = digest(\"snapshot\", graphDoc, GRAPH_DATA_SNAPSHOT_C1_PROFILE);",
      "ts/src/evaluator/evaluate.ts:62": "  readonly checkpoint: string;",
      "ts/src/evaluator/evaluate.ts:150": "  const checkpoint = checkpointIdentity(theta);",
      "ts/src/cli/rpc-sample.ts:178": "    const probe = { program_digest: programHex, parameters } as never;",
      "ts/src/cli/eval-run.ts:476": "  const identities = { program: receipt.program_digest, checkpoint: receipt.checkpoint_digest };",
      "ts/src/cli/inspect-decision.ts:161": "const DECISION_IDENTITY_FIELDS = [\"graph_digest\", \"program_digest\", \"checkpoint_digest\"] as const;",
      "ts/src/cli/sample-command.ts:312": "      snapshotDigest: bare(d.graph_digest),",
      "ts/src/cli/sample-command.ts:314": "      checkpointDigest: unqualifyDigest(d.checkpoint_digest, \"checkpoint\"),",
      "ts/src/evaluator/receipt.ts:30": "  readonly checkpoint: string;",
      "ts/src/artifact-store/cas.ts:71": "  readonly digest: string;"
    },
